  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 101 AM MST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nTrailing energy drops into the 4 corners region Friday night keeping \nsome light snow showers going across the southwest mountains before \nthe system moves across CO on Saturday as an open wave of varying \namplitudes.  Overall, moisture appears lacking and any precipitation \nmay be brief, spotty and light across the southeast plains, if\nit happens at all, on Saturday. The Palmer Divide and Raton \nridge could see some light snow, though any accumulations would \nbe brief and confined to the grassy and cold surfaces.\n\nThe system pulls away to the east Saturday night with a chilly night \nexpected into Sunday morning. Lows may drop into the single \ndigits across some of the mountains/valley locations, with 20s \nacross the lower elevations. \n\nTemperatures will remain below normal for Sunday into next week with \nthe active weather pattern continuing as a parade of upper \ntroughs move through westerly flow aloft. Sunday will be dry, \nbut snow showers could return to portions of the area later \nMonday into Tuesday. There is low confidence on these details as\nthe system looks pretty open and progressive in the 00z \noperational runs. But this could change with future runs. \nAnother storm system is expected for late week with even greater\nuncertainty on timing, strength and track.",
